      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree cf5eadcb6b2723e539e4eee5dc3f1b3c6164ccf1\nparent cce32b16874e85e8a00cfa1a2190f0b6f4dcaf66\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792102639 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792105204 +0200\n\nwallet: cleanse the hasher in BytesToKeySHA512AES\n\nAfter the loop, the CSHA512 `di` still holds the derived key and IV in\nits state, and the previous round's digest in its buffer. `buf` is\ncleansed before the function returns, but `di` is left on the stack.\n\nCleanse it the same way as the `hkdf` object in the BIP324 cipher.\n",
